Apple’s San Francisco font family (including SF Pro Display and SF Pro Text) is proprietary[3]. It is provided by Apple primarily for designing and developing applications for Apple platforms (iOS, iPadOS, macOS, watchOS, tvOS)[4]. If you are using it for commercial web projects or non-Apple branding outside of platform guidelines, be sure to review Apple's official design and trademark guidelines.

